  "description": "Wisconsin's 6th Congressional District, covering east-central Wisconsin including Oshkosh, Sheboygan, and Fond du Lac, is a safely Republican seat held by incumbent Glenn Grothman (R) since 2015. The 2026 race features a competitive Republican primary between Grothman and challenger Jonathan Peetz, a crowded seven-candidate Democratic primary, and independent candidates including union fire captain Mike Thurow and Elizabeth Fitzgibbon. The district has not elected a Democrat to Congress since 1964, but independent candidate Thurow has shown surprising strength in early polling, cutting Grothman's lead significantly in head-to-head matchups.",
